---
import GovLayout from '../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
import PhaseBanner from '../components/PhaseBanner.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import SummaryBox from '../components/SummaryBox.astro';
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro';
import InsetText from '../components/InsetText.astro';
import WarningText from '../components/WarningText.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Fiscal Policy Analysis" department="Ministry of Finance & Treasury" description="Supplementary fiscal analysis — balance distribution, tax vs interest crossover, and projected revenue based on real Bank of ASEAN account data.">

<PhaseBanner tag="Analysis" text="Supplementary data — 24 March 2026" />
<Breadcrumbs items={[
  { label: "Fiscal Policy", href: "/fiscal-policy" },
  { label: "Analysis", href: "/fiscal-analysis" },
]} />

<main class="govuk-main-wrapper">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">

    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1>Fiscal Policy Analysis</h1>

      <SummaryBox title="About this page">
        <p>This page contains supplementary analysis of the <a href="/fiscal-policy">Fiscal Policy</a>, including current wealth distribution, tax vs interest crossover modelling, and projected revenue with balance decay. Data sourced from Bank of ASEAN accounts as at 24 March 2026.</p>
      </SummaryBox>

      <!-- 1. Balance Tier Impact -->
      <h2 id="balance-tiers">1. Balance Tier Impact</h2>
      <p>The following table shows the monthly wealth tax for a player who remains idle for 30 days straight, broken down by starting balance tier:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Table 1: Monthly wealth tax by balance tier (30 days idle)</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Starting Balance</th><th>Monthly Tax</th><th>Effective Rate</th><th>Remaining</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$1,000,000</td><td>$1,896</td><td>0.2%</td><td>$1,121,703</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$5,000,000</td><td>$116,753</td><td>2.3%</td><td>$5,498,657</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$10,000,000</td><td>$260,112</td><td>2.6%</td><td>$10,953,384</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$20,000,000</td><td>$553,127</td><td>2.8%</td><td>$21,300,683</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$50,000,000</td><td>$1,835,929</td><td>3.7%</td><td>$50,309,066</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$100,000,000</td><td>$3,933,184</td><td>3.9%</td><td>$97,310,602</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$200,000,000</td><td>$10,071,843</td><td>5.0%</td><td>$190,143,428</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <!-- 2. Tax vs Interest Crossover -->
      <h2 id="crossover">2. Tax vs Interest Crossover</h2>
      <p>The following table shows how many days of continuous idleness it takes for <strong>cumulative wealth tax to exceed cumulative interest earned</strong>. Beyond this point, the account is in net decline.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Table 2: Days offline until cumulative wealth tax exceeds cumulative interest</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Balance</th><th>Crossover</th><th>Observation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$1,000,000</td><td>Never</td><td style="text-align:left">Exempt from wealth tax (at threshold)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$5,000,000</td><td>Never</td><td style="text-align:left">Interest always exceeds tax — Low bracket (k=0.65)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$10,000,000</td><td>Never</td><td style="text-align:left">Interest always exceeds tax — Low bracket</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$20,000,000</td><td style="color:#d4a910;font-weight:700">~63 days</td><td style="text-align:left">Enters Mid bracket (k=1.05); interest scaling begins</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$30,000,000</td><td style="color:#d4a910;font-weight:700">~32 days</td><td style="text-align:left">Interest scaling (60% rate) + Mid bracket</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$50,000,000</td><td style="color:#d4351c;font-weight:700">~16 days</td><td style="text-align:left">Interest scaling (37% rate) + Mid bracket</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$100,000,000</td><td style="color:#d4351c;font-weight:700">~5 days</td><td style="text-align:left">Full bracket range; interest scaling (11% rate)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$200,000,000</td><td style="color:#d4351c;font-weight:700">&lt;1 day</td><td style="text-align:left">Interest effectively zero (2% scale)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        Below $20M, interest always outpaces the wealth tax — the system is net-positive for smaller accounts regardless of activity. Above $20M, inactivity becomes increasingly punitive as both the tax brackets and the interest scaling work against idle wealth.
      </InsetText>

      <!-- 3. Projected Revenue -->
      <h2 id="projected-revenue">3. Projected Revenue</h2>
      <p>The following projections use <strong>real account data</strong> from the Bank of ASEAN (as at 24 March 2026) and simulate hour-by-hour tax collection with balance decay. Assumptions: <strong>15% daily active rate</strong> (players who log in reset their offline clock), no new deposits.</p>

      <h3>3.1 Current Account Distribution</h3>
      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Table 3: Account distribution (922 accounts, $4.89B total)</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Bracket</th><th>Accounts</th><th>Total Balance</th><th>% of Wealth</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">Under $1M (exempt)</td><td>685</td><td>$115,000,000</td><td>2.4%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$1M – $20M (Low)</td><td>174</td><td>$791,000,000</td><td>16.2%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$20M – $100M (Mid)</td><td>51</td><td>$1,753,000,000</td><td>35.8%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$100M+ (High)</td><td>12</td><td>$2,230,000,000</td><td>45.6%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <WarningText>
        <strong>Key observation:</strong> 81% of the nation's wealth is held in accounts above the Mid bracket threshold ($20M+). These accounts are the primary source of wealth tax revenue — and are also subject to the steepest interest scaling (60%–2% effective interest rate).
      </WarningText>

      <h3>3.2 12-Month Revenue Projection</h3>
      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Table 4: Projected wealth tax revenue (with balance decay)</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Tax Collected</th><th>Avg Daily</th><th>Remaining Taxable Balance</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>$187,008,063</td><td>$6,233,602</td><td>$5,105,208,568</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>$140,105,277</td><td>$4,670,176</td><td>$4,965,103,291</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>$131,285,373</td><td>$4,376,179</td><td>$4,833,817,918</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">4</td><td>$140,685,647</td><td>$4,689,522</td><td>$4,693,132,271</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">6</td><td>$118,126,882</td><td>$3,937,563</td><td>$4,431,641,251</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">9</td><td>$111,671,151</td><td>$3,722,372</td><td>$4,082,308,280</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">12</td><td>$117,608,637</td><td>$3,920,288</td><td>$3,761,728,182</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="formula">
        12-month projected total: $1,530,488,449<br /><br />
        Taxable pool reduction: 28.9% ($5.29B → $3.76B)
      </div>

      <InsetText>
        Revenue declines over time as the taxable pool shrinks — this is by design. The wealth tax is self-limiting: as idle balances are eroded, the remaining accounts contribute less, and the system naturally approaches an equilibrium where tax revenue matches new wealth creation from active economic activity.
      </InsetText>

    </div>

    <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-third">
      <Sidebar items={[
        { label: "Balance Tier Impact", href: "#balance-tiers" },
        { label: "Tax vs Interest Crossover", href: "#crossover" },
        { label: "Projected Revenue", href: "#projected-revenue" },
      ]} />
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</GovLayout>
